cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use DA-YOLO in your research, please cite the software
  as below. Also cite the foundational works listed under references.

title: "DA-YOLO: Deformable Attention YOLO for Small-Object Detection in Remote Sensing and Drone Imagery"
type: software

authors:
  - family-names: Tiadi
    given-names: Aditya
    github: https://github.com/Aditya3815

repository-code: https://github.com/Aditya3815/DASwin-YOLO
license: AGPL-3.0
version: "2.0.0"
date-released: "2025-06-01"

abstract: >-
  DA-YOLO (Deformable Attention YOLO) is a novel object detection architecture
  extending YOLOv5s with five principled improvements for dense small-object
  detection: (1) DC3SWT — Multi-Scale Deformable Attention replacing fixed-window
  Swin attention (W-MSA+SW-MSA) in both backbone P5 and all PANet neck levels;
  (2) WIoU v1 geometric box regression loss; (3) SE-BiFPN — BiFPN cross-scale
  neck with Squeeze-Excitation channel recalibration at all 6 fusion nodes;
  (4) CoordAttMulti — per-scale Coordinate Attention injected before each
  detection head; (5) 4-scale detection head (P2–P5, strides 4/8/16/32).
  Benchmarked on VisDrone2019-DET (30.85% mAP@0.5 with SAHI), DIOR-R
  (60.00% mAP@0.5), and DOTA 1.5 (33.33% mAP@0.5). All components implemented
  in pure PyTorch — no custom CUDA extensions required.

keywords:
  - object-detection
  - small-object-detection
  - swin-transformer
  - deformable-attention
  - YOLO
  - remote-sensing
  - BiFPN
  - deep-learning

references:
  - type: article
    title: >-
      Swin-Transformer-Based YOLOv5 for Small-Object Detection in
      Remote Sensing Images
    authors:
      - family-names: Cao
        given-names: Yangxintong
      - family-names: Lv
        given-names: Zhijia
      - family-names: Xie
        given-names: Liangjian
    journal: Sensors
    volume: 23
    issue: 7
    year: 2023
    doi: 10.3390/s23073634
    url: https://doi.org/10.3390/s23073634
    notes: >-
      This work is the direct inspiration for the C3SWT baseline
      (fixed-window Swin blocks) that DA-YOLO extends and improves upon.

  - type: conference-paper
    title: "Deformable DETR: Deformable Transformers for End-to-End Object Detection"
    authors:
      - family-names: Zhu
        given-names: Xizhou
      - family-names: Su
        given-names: Weijie
      - family-names: Lu
        given-names: Lewei
      - family-names: Li
        given-names: Bin
      - family-names: Wang
        given-names: Xiaogang
      - family-names: Dai
        given-names: Jifeng
    collection-title: "International Conference on Learning Representations (ICLR 2021)"
    year: 2021
    url: https://arxiv.org/abs/2010.04159
    notes: >-
      The Multi-Scale Deformable Attention (MSDA) mechanism that DC3SWT
      is derived from. DA-YOLO adapts MSDA for single-scale feature
      maps within a YOLOv5-style backbone, implemented in pure PyTorch.

  - type: article
    title: "Wise-IoU: Bounding Box Regression Loss with Dynamic Focusing Mechanism"
    authors:
      - family-names: Tong
        given-names: Zanjia
    journal: "AAAI 2023"
    year: 2023
    url: https://arxiv.org/abs/2301.10051
    notes: >-
      WIoU v1 geometric focusing loss used in DA-YOLO for down-weighting
      easy anchors and concentrating gradient on geometrically hard predictions.

  - type: software
    title: "YOLOv5 by Ultralytics"
    authors:
      - family-names: Jocher
        given-names: Glenn
        orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5950-6979"
    version: 7.0
    doi: 10.5281/zenodo.3908559
    date-released: "2020-05-29"
    license: AGPL-3.0
    url: https://github.com/ultralytics/yolov5
    notes: >-
      DA-YOLO is built on top of the YOLOv5 training framework.
      The backbone, data pipeline, loss functions, and training loop
      are derived from this codebase.
